<!-- Hero -->
<section style="background:var(--bg-warm);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding-block:3.5rem 3rem;">
  <div class="wrapper">
    <p class="section-label">Coffee Origin Trip · Trip Report</p>
    <h1 style="max-width:640px;margin-bottom:.75rem;">Uganda, May 2–10, 2026</h1>
    <p style="font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--fg-mid);max-width:640px;margin-bottom:1rem;">
      A delegation of eight German coffee professionals — roasters, an importer, a trader, and an analyst — travelled to Uganda for nine days of farm visits, cuppings, and direct trade meetings. The trip was organised by the German Embassy Kampala and Uganda's Ministry of Agriculture, Animal Industry and Fisheries (MAAIF), with logistical coordination by Zuricaf and the Uganda-side team.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--fg-light);max-width:640px;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      The delegation visited research stations, primary processing facilities, cooperatives, and high-altitude farms across six growing regions, and held two structured cupping sessions. All eight participants completed the post-trip survey — read the highlights below.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-group" style="justify-content:flex-start;">
      <a href="/lot-info/" class="btn">Register as Supplier →</a>
      <a href="https://calendar.notion.so/meet/lorenzstckert/h932i4pxy" class="btn btn-outline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a call</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

