      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Programme teaser / gated request -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrapper" style="max-width:640px;">
    <p class="section-label">Programme</p>
    <h2 style="margin-bottom:.5rem;">Full Day-by-Day Programme</h2>
    <p style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--fg-mid);margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      The detailed itinerary — stations visited, processing methods, and cupping notes by region — is available on request for delegation participants and prospective roasting partners. Leave your details and we'll send you straight to it.
    </p>

    <form name="uganda-programme-request" method="POST" netlify netlify-honeypot="bot-field" action="/uganda-2026-programm/">
      <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="uganda-programme-request">
      <p style="display:none;"><label>Don't fill this out: <input name="bot-field"></label></p>

      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem 1.5rem;margin-bottom:1rem;">
        <div>
          <label class="c-label" for="up_name">Name <span style="color:var(--accent)">*</span></label>
          <input id="up_name" name="name" type="text" required placeholder="Your name" class="c-input">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label class="c-label" for="up_email">Email <span style="color:var(--accent)">*</span></label>
          <input id="up_email" name="email" type="email" required placeholder="your@email.com" class="c-input">
        </div>
      </div>
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Vollständiges Programm anfragen →</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Survey results -->
<section class="section section-bg">
  <div class="wrapper">
    <p class="section-label">Participant Survey · Wave 1</p>
    <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem;">What the delegation told us</h2>
    <p style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--fg-mid);max-width:680px;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      All eight participants completed the post-trip survey (100% response rate). Six of eight got actionable information from most or all sessions — a strong result for a nine-day trip with a mixed cohort. The most consistent format requests for the next trip:
    </p>
    <ul style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--fg-mid);max-width:680px;line-height:1.7;padding-left:1.2rem;">
      <li><strong>More cuppings</strong> — 7 of 8 respondents want 3–4 cupping sessions spread across the trip, not concentrated at the end.</li>
      <li><strong>A standardised producer list after each cupping</strong> — directly addressed by the ongoing Zuricaf lot-info collection process.</li>
      <li><strong>Less travel time</strong> — grab-and-go meals instead of sit-down lunches to free up afternoon session time.</li>
      <li><strong>Rest and processing breaks</strong> — a station break every 2–3 days to synthesise impressions commercially.</li>
      <li><strong>A slightly longer trip</strong> — 10–11 days rather than compressing the same content into 9, with a lighter final day.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Group photo -->
<section style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
